% expect-output: 440.0
% expect-output: 404.0
% expect-output: -468.68045
% expect-output: 404.0
% expect-output: -463.33493
% expect-output: 503.71344
% Scenario: tangent points at a rotated corner. An acute corner whose
% tangent points lie some 930 units out amplifies any error in the
% corner's angle; the current point is read back exactly and the
% tangent distance is computed in double precision, so the readings
% agree with the exact ones (-468.680446, 404, -463.334916, 503.713432)
% to six significant digits, which is the precision the harness compares
% numbers at. The current point, then the two tangent points, x before
% y, one value per line.
-45 rotate 440 404 moveto
currentpoint exch = =
464 404 371 414 50 arcto
4 -1 roll = 3 -1 roll = exch = =
stroke showpage
